virglrenderer: Venus asks the host about the LINEAR modifier with INPUT_ATTACHMENT

What: neither Mac Vulkan driver (KosmicKrisp, MoltenVK) has
VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier, so vkr answers the guest's questions about
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR with the host's answer for VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR. That
question left out COLOR_ATTACHMENT and INPUT_ATTACHMENT. It now leaves out only
COLOR_ATTACHMENT, and only for a format whose optimal tiling renders
(vkr_physical_device_linear_usage, which virgl-venus-image-limits.patch uses too).
Why: Zink (OpenGL on Vulkan) asks for its shared render targets with
SAMPLED|TRANSFER|COLOR_ATTACHMENT|INPUT_ATTACHMENT and the LINEAR modifier. It was
told "supported" and made one. KosmicKrisp makes every 2D image with
INPUT_ATTACHMENT a 2D array texture, linear ones too, and Metal ends the process
at vkBindImageMemory2 for a linear 2D array ("Linear texture: must be of type
MTLTextureType2D"): a program in the VM (glxinfo or Ghostty with Zink, #598) took
the whole VM down. KosmicKrisp's own answer to the full question is "not
supported"; only the shortened question got a yes.
COLOR_ATTACHMENT stays out where optimal tiling renders: the Mac drivers never
claim linear colour attachments, yet a guest's window buffers are linear colour
attachments and render on both. Every format the shortened question accepts was
made LINEAR with COLOR_ATTACHMENT and bound without an abort (KosmicKrisp 57
formats, MoltenVK 56, M4 macOS 27). For a format whose optimal tiling cannot
render, the question keeps COLOR_ATTACHMENT and is refused.
Upstream: the emulation is the startergo tap's (homebrew-virglrenderer,
virglrenderer-macos-unified.patch at de31b78a), not freedesktop's. Not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-image-limits.c (build time, real drivers, one child
per case): Zink's image made through vkr's dispatch ends the child on
KosmicKrisp without this patch and virgl-venus-image-limits.patch; with them the
query answers VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED and vkCreateImage refuses it.

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.c b/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.c
index 381b319..c1001a1 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.c
@@ -396,6 +396,28 @@ vkr_physical_device_init_queue_family_properties(struct vkr_physical_device *phy
    physical_dev->queue_family_properties = props;
 }
 
+/* OmacVM: the usage to ask the host about for a LINEAR image. The Mac drivers never
+ * claim linear COLOR_ATTACHMENT, yet single-layer linear colour images render on both
+ * (a guest's window buffers are such images), so COLOR_ATTACHMENT is left out of the
+ * question, but only for a format whose optimal tiling renders: for any other the
+ * question keeps it and is refused. INPUT_ATTACHMENT stays in: KosmicKrisp makes a
+ * texture with it a 2D array, which Metal refuses for linear memory with an abort (Zink's
+ * shared render targets, #598). virgl-venus-image-limits.patch asks the same. */
+VkImageUsageFlags
+vkr_physical_device_linear_usage(struct vkr_physical_device *physical_dev,
+                                 VkFormat format,
+                                 VkImageUsageFlags usage)
+{
+   if (!(usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT))
+      return usage;
+   VkFormatProperties props = { 0 };
+   physical_dev->proc_table.GetPhysicalDeviceFormatProperties(
+      physical_dev->base.handle.physical_device, format, &props);
+   if (props.optimalTilingFeatures & VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT)
+      usage &= ~VK_IMAGE_USAGE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT;
+   return usage;
+}
+
 static void
 vkr_physical_device_emulate_drm_props(VkDrmFormatModifierPropertiesListEXT *drm_props_list)
 {
@@ -835,8 +857,8 @@ vkr_dispatch_vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2(
             prev_struct->pNext = drm_format_mod->pNext;
             vkr_log("emulating DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR with VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR");
             pImageFormatInfo->tiling = VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR;
-            pImageFormatInfo->usage &=
-               ~(VK_IMAGE_USAGE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT | VK_IMAGE_USAGE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_BIT);
+            pImageFormatInfo->usage = vkr_physical_device_linear_usage(
+               physical_dev, pImageFormatInfo->format, pImageFormatInfo->usage);
          } else {
             vkr_log("only DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR is supported");
             args->ret = VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED;
diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.h b/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.h
index ce2b80c..251cbd0 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.h
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.h
@@ -51,6 +51,12 @@ VKR_DEFINE_OBJECT_CAST(physical_device, VK_OBJECT_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE, VkPhysic
 void
 vkr_context_init_physical_device_dispatch(struct vkr_context *ctx);
 
+/* OmacVM: the usage to ask the host about for a LINEAR image (see the .c file) */
+VkImageUsageFlags
+vkr_physical_device_linear_usage(struct vkr_physical_device *physical_dev,
+                                 VkFormat format,
+                                 VkImageUsageFlags usage);
+
 void
 vkr_physical_device_destroy(struct vkr_context *ctx,
                             struct vkr_physical_device *physical_dev);
